===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|institution or place for exhibition or conservation}} An [[institution]], [[building#Noun|building]], or [[room#Noun|room]] for the [[exhibition]] and [[conservation]] of important objects, especially [[work of art|works of art]].
#: {{hypo|en|art gallery}}
#: {{cot|en|museum}}
#: {{ux|en|In the '''gallery''' are displayed genuine artifacts dug up from the site, and in the gift shop you can buy a replica as a souvenir.}}
#: {{ux|en|Some of her work is so impressive that it really ought to be in a '''gallery'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Letha Ch'ien|title=This stunning de Young exhibition transforms the museum’s African galleries|journal=w:San Francisco Chronicle|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260908230256/https://www.sfchronicle.com/entertainment/arts-exhibits/article/nengi-omuku-de-young-sf-22391676.php|date=8 September 2026|passage=The works can be seen from all sides because they hang freely in the '''galleries''' rather than against walls, creating an immersive environment that feels less like a conventional exhibition than a gathering of its own.}}
# {{senseid|en|establishment for display and trade}} An [[establishment]] that [[buy#Verb|buy]]s, [[sell]]s, and [[display#Verb|display]]s works of art.
#: {{cot|en|gallerist<alt:gallerist's>}}
#: {{nearsyn|en|art dealer<alt:art dealer's>|dealer<alt:dealer's>}}
#: {{ux|en|Some of her best work can be yours: it is available at a '''gallery''', if you can afford it.}}
# {{senseid|en|part of a theater or auditorium}} The [[uppermost]] [[seating]] [[area]] projecting from the rear or side walls of a [[theater]], [[concert hall]], or [[auditorium]].
#: {{hypo|en|peanut gallery}}
#: {{ux|en|We could afford the less expensive seats in the '''gallery'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|spectators at an event, metonymically}} {{lb|en|by extension|metonym}} The [[spectator]]s at an [[event]], collectively.
#: {{hypo|en|peanut gallery}}
#: {{collocation|en|The politician was clearly appealing to the '''gallery'''}}
#* {{quote-web
